# 3Q Facility Dashboard — clinerules
#
# Single source of project-specific rules for a coding agent. Read
# `.graphify/GRAPH_REPORT.md` for architecture review; run `graphify update .`
# after edits to keep it current.

# 1. TECH STACK BOUNDARIES
# Monorepo topology: TWO INDEPENDENT packages, no root package.json, no npm
# workspaces. Commands ALWAYS run per-package (cd into the package first).
#
# client/  (label-erp-client)
#   React 18.3.1 · TS 5.9.3 · Vite 5.4.21 · Vitest 4.1.10
#   shadcn/ui base-nova (Radix + @base-ui/react both installed)
#   TanStack Query 5.101.2 · TanStack Table 8.21.3
#   react-hook-form 7.81.0 · @hookform/resolvers 5.4.0 · zod 4.4.3
#   zustand 5.0.14 · axios 1.18 · date-fns 4.4 · recharts 3.8 · sonner 1.5
#   lucide-react · cmdk · xlsx 0.18 · canvas-confetti
#   Tests: vitest + jsdom 29 + @testing-library/react 16.3 + jest-dom 7
#   Path alias: @/* -> src/*
#
# server/  (label-erp-server)
#   Node engines 24.x (NOTE: CI pins Node 20 — fix or align) · TS 5.9.3
#   Express 4.22.2 · Drizzle ORM 0.36.4 + drizzle-kit 0.30 (postgres 3.4)
#   Supabase PostgreSQL · zod 3.25.76 · tsup 8.5 · tsx 4.19 · vitest 4.1.10
#   helmet · cors · compression · express-rate-limit 8.6.1 · nodemailer 9
#   Path aliases: @api/* | @db/* | @config/*
#
# ⚠ Zod divergence: client zod v4 vs server zod v3. Zod SCHEMA objects are NOT
#   portable between packages (v4 changed error-message syntax, deprecations).
#   Share only TS types; never runtime schema objects across packages.
# Do not add a dependency without confirming it is genuinely missing from the
# version list above and that the installed version matches.

# 2. CODE STYLE & QUALITY
# Frontend
# - Feature layout: features/<feature>/{pages,components,hooks,services,schemas,types.ts}.
# - Hooks (use-<resource>.ts): export a <RESOURCE>_KEYS query-key factory; read
#   hooks use select: (res) => res.data to unwrap the {data} envelope; mutations
#   invalidateQueries + toast.success/error. Copy this shape exactly.
# - Services: thin async wrappers over lib/api.ts — endpoint + type mapping only.
# - Forms: react-hook-form + zodResolver. The ONLY accepted `any` is
#   `zodResolver(schema) as any` (resolvers v5 generic-inference workaround).
# - Use AppButton/AppInput/AppSelect/AppCard/AppDialog in feature code; reach for
#   a raw shadcn primitive only when no App* wrapper exists. Before hand-writing
#   a UI component, check the live registry: npx shadcn@latest add <name>.
# - Server state via TanStack Query ONLY; Zustand is for UI theme state only.
# Backend
# - layers: routes -> controllers -> services -> repositories.
#   controllers: one service call, shape response, asyncHandler-wrapped.
#   services: existence checks, cross-entity validation, number->String for
#     Drizzle decimal columns before passing to repositories.
#   repositories: raw Drizzle query builders only, return raw rows.
# - Validation: Zod in api/validations/<resource>.validation.ts;
#   validateRequest stashes on req.validatedBody/Params/Query (never mutate
#   req.body directly); query-only schemas are flat. Controllers read via
#   (req.validatedX ?? req.X) fallback.
# - Errors: throw ApiError subclasses from services; controllers stay thin.
# - Decimal columns are strings over the wire — Number(...) before arithmetic.
# - Path aliases: @api/* | @db/* | @config/* inside server/src; @/* client.
# - Strict mode on both packages; keep zero TS errors.
# Tests
# - Write strict unit tests for any modified logic. `npm test` after editing.
# - typecheck in the touched package (`npm run typecheck`, tsc --noEmit).

# 3. PRODUCTION PIPELINE RULES
# One order runs exactly ONE workflow, selected by productType: "printed"|"woven".
# PRINTED: Planning -> Printing -> Cutting -> Packaging -> Dispatch  (units: rolls)
# WOVEN:   Planning -> Weaving  -> Cutting -> Packaging -> Dispatch  (units: pieces)
# Cutting and packaging are ORDER-SCOPED on the live DB (a batch spans label types,
# so BOTH line columns are NULL and numbering restarts per order + stage). Enforced
# by CHECK production_batches_first_stage_one_line (first stages: num_nonulls(...) = 1;
# cutting/packaging: num_nonulls(...) = 0) and the unique index
# production_batches_order_stage_no_uq.
# CORRECTED 2026-09-26: migration 0023_revert_cutting_packaging_line_scope.sql AND the
# schema.ts production_batches_one_line check (num_nonulls(...) = 1 for every stage)
# describe a LINE-SCOPED variant that was recorded as applied but NEVER executed, and
# matches neither the live schema nor the running code. Keep-order-scoped vs
# move-to-line-scoped is an open product decision — read
# memory-bank/migration-reconciliation.md before touching either.
# production_stage_tx_type (append-only, ordered):
#   print_credit -> cut_consume_print/cut_credit -> package_consume_cut/package_credit
# - Printing/Weaving only CREDIT their stage.
# - Cut consumes the stage above + credits its own; Package consumes cut + credits.
# - Waste is allowed ONLY at the FIRST stage (printing or weaving) — enforced.
# - Packaging batches have an operator but NO machine — enforced.
# - Only COMPLETED batches count toward stage totals; CANCELLED never moves counts.
# - Never hand-write server-calculated production fields on the client.

# 4. ROLES & SECURITY
# REAL state: NO authentication and NO RBAC in the code. JWT_SECRET is commented
# out in server/src/config/env.ts; grepping src for jsonwebtoken|passport|req.user
# returns nothing. The user_role enum is descriptive only and actorUserId is an
# optional attribution field, NOT an authorization signal — do not treat it as
# auth. Do NOT invent a CEO/Initiator/Accountant matrix — it does not exist here.
#
# user_role enum (server/src/db/tables/users.table.ts):
#   office_staff         — office staff; work-order master data
#   production_manager   — production planning + machine/operator assignment
#   production_operator  — operates machines; packaging is done by this role
#   (deliberately no packaging-specific role.)
# apiRateLimiter (express-rate-limit) IS active: 1000 req/IP/min on /api.
# authRateLimiter is pre-wired for when auth arrives (unused today).
# CORS_ORIGIN is a comma-separated allow-list; "*" is rejected loudly in prod.

# 5. VERCEL / SERVERLESS DEPLOYMENT
# TWO VERCEL PROJECTS: server (Root Directory=server) and client
# (Root Directory=client). Deploy server first, then client, then lock CORS down.
# Server build (package.json "build"): tsup bundles src/api-entry.ts -> api/, then
# renames api/api-entry.js -> api/index.js. vercel.json exposes
# functions["api/index.js"] (maxDuration 30, regions ["bom1"]) and rewrites
# everything to /api. NOTE the compiled bundle (server/api/index.js) is checked
# into the repo — keep it in sync with `npm run build` before pushing.
# Runtime DB: DATABASE_URL = Supabase transaction pooler (6543, prepare:false).
# DIRECT_URL (session pooler :5432) is for migrations/DDL from a dev machine ONLY.
#
# DATABASE PROVISIONING — the migration chain CANNOT be replayed from 0000
# (0018 ALTERs a table only 0019 creates; live also has objects no migration makes).
# New/empty DBs are provisioned from a pg_dump baseline instead — see
# server/scripts/baseline/README.md and memory-bank/migration-reconciliation.md:
#   npm run db:baseline          # refresh scripts/baseline/live-schema.sql from live
#   psql "$URL" -f scripts/baseline/live-schema.sql
#   node --env-file <env> scripts/reconcile-migrations.mjs --fresh
#   npx drizzle-kit migrate      # applies ONLY genuinely-new migrations
# Replaying 0000–0024 is an audit path only, never the provisioning path.

# 6. KNOWLEDGE GRAPH / TOOLING
# - Prefer `graphify query|path|explain` over raw grep. Report lives at
#   `.graphify/GRAPH_REPORT.md` (NOT the old graphify-out/ path).
# - After modifying code: `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost).
# - Run typecheck + tests in BOTH packages (CI runs them independently, on Node 20).

# 7. MEMORY BANK
# - Read memory-bank/{projectbrief,activeContext,progress}.md before work.
# - Update activeContext.md and progress.md after changes; keep projectbrief.md
#   stable (only change when goals/invariants genuinely shift).
# - Treat CLAUDE.md as PARTIALLY STALE (predates woven/thread/dyeing/batch-flow;
#   still claims rate limiter is a no-op); verify against code, never contradict it.
# - Verify before trusting: run `npm run typecheck` + `npm test` + `npm run build`
#   in the relevant package; align CI (Node 20) with engines (Node 24) at some point.
# Strict Dependency & Runtime Version Constraints

## Client Package (`/client` - React 18, TanStack Query v5, Zod v4)
- **TanStack Query v5 Rules:**
  - ALWAYS use single-object options syntax: `useQuery({ queryKey: [...], queryFn: ... })`.
  - NEVER write `onSuccess`, `onError`, or `onSettled` inside `useQuery` or `useInfiniteQuery` (these do not exist in v5).
  - Use `isPending` for initial loading states rather than `isLoading`.
  - Use `gcTime` instead of `cacheTime`.
- **Zod v4 Rules:**
  - Keep client Zod schemas isolated within `/client/src/lib/validations` or `/client/src/schemas`.
  - Do NOT import Zod schemas directly across the `/client` and `/server` boundary to avoid Zod 4 vs Zod 3 runtime type mismatches.

## Server Package (`/server` - Node 24, Express, Drizzle ORM, Zod v3)
- **Node 24 Runtime Rules:**
  - Do NOT import or initialize `dotenv` in server code—Node handles environment variables via `--env-file .env` at CLI startup.
  - Rely on global `fetch` and native Web APIs; do not install or import `node-fetch` or `axios` in the server package.
- **Zod v3 Rules:**
  - Keep server validation schemas inside `/server/src/schemas` using standard Zod 3 syntax.